# Mock scenario engine

The mock-up has no backend. All screens read static fixtures through one `DataSource` interface, and "streaming" is a scripted playback with fixed timings, so the demo is identical every run. The backend team replaces `MockDataSource` with `ApiDataSource` later without touching components.

## 1. File layout

```
src/
  data/
    types.ts            # contracts below; keep in sync with the backend's Pydantic models
    DataSource.ts       # interface
    MockDataSource.ts   # fixtures + playback
    ApiDataSource.ts    # typed stub with TODOs
  fixtures/
    checks.ts           # the 6 legacy checks and their stages
    source.ts           # plugin invocation, commands.cfg, services.cfg, contacts.cfg as strings
    ruleCards.ts        # rule card for check_rack_inlet (+ the flagged variant)
    recording.ts        # 21-day series generator (seeded) for B7, neighbours, CU-B, row C, A4
    findings.ts         # the six findings, with evidence series refs
    verify.ts           # coverage runs, traces, counterexamples, rounds, certificate (see verification-ui)
    scripts.ts          # playback scripts: Read, Find, Prove step timings
  engine/
    prng.ts             # mulberry32(seed)
    playback.ts         # runs a script: emits events on a schedule; supports jumpToEnd, restart
  state/
    store.tsx           # context + reducer; subscribes to DataSource
```

## 2. Contracts (`types.ts`)

```ts
export type CheckStage = 'audit'|'parallel_run'|'verified'|'signed_off'|'retired'|'blocked'|'drop';
export interface LegacyCheck { id: string; name: string; plugin: string; watches: string; stage: CheckStage; findings?: { total: number; accepted: number }; coverage?: { done: number; total: number }; traces?: { done: number; total: number }; openCounterexamples: number; blockedReason?: string; dropReason?: string; }

export interface SourceRange { file: string; from: number; to: number; }
export interface RuleCardStatement { id: string; section: 'checks'|'thresholds'|'pages_when'|'pages_who'|'ignores'; text: string; source: SourceRange[]; verification?: { status: 'pending'|'running'|'verified'|'flagged'; runs: { input: string; legacy: string; expected: string; ok: boolean }[]; note?: string; corrected?: string }; }
export interface RuleCard { checkId: string; model: 'Nemotron Super'; statements: RuleCardStatement[]; mode: 'live'|'cached'|'mock'; }

export interface Series { id: string; unit: string; points: { t: number; v: number | null }[]; threshold?: number; }
export interface Finding { id: number; severity: 'critical'|'warning'|'watch'|'info'; title: string; sentences: string; detector: string; detectorNumbers: Record<string, string | number>; action: string; target: { kind: 'rack'|'unit'|'row'|'config'; id: string }; evidence: { series: string[]; caption: string }; status: 'open'|'accepted'|'dismissed'; decision?: { by: string; at: string; reason?: string; workOrderId?: string }; model: 'Nemotron Nano'; mode: 'live'|'cached'|'mock'; }
export interface ReplaySummary { checkId: string; days: number; pluginRuns: number; legacyPages: number; sameFalseAlarm: number; pageTicks: number[]; detectorHits: { t: number; findingId: number }[]; }
export interface WorkOrder { id: string; number: number; title: string; labels: string[]; unit: string; location: string; likelyPart: string; body: string; evidenceUrl: string; createdBy: string; at: string; }
export interface Handoff { shift: string; writtenBy: string; reviewedBy?: string; accepted: { finding: Finding; workOrder: WorkOrder; owner: string; eta: string; watch: string }[]; dismissed: Finding[]; signedOff: string[]; timeline: { at: string; text: string }[]; acknowledgedBy?: string; acknowledgedAt?: string; }

export interface PlaybackStep { id: string; at: number; /* ms from start */ label: string; model?: 'Nemotron Super'|'Nemotron Nano'; tool?: string; durationMs?: number; emits?: EngineEvent; }
export type EngineEvent =
  | { type: 'step'; screen: 'read'|'find'|'prove'; step: PlaybackStep; status: 'running'|'done'|'error' }
  | { type: 'ruleCard'; data: RuleCard }
  | { type: 'statementVerified'; statementId: string; verification: RuleCardStatement['verification'] }
  | { type: 'replay'; data: ReplaySummary }
  | { type: 'finding'; data: Finding }
  | { type: 'verify'; data: import('./verifyTypes').VerifyResult }   // see verification-ui
  | { type: 'round'; round: number; open: number }
  | { type: 'certificate'; data: import('./verifyTypes').Certificate }
  | { type: 'handoff'; data: Handoff };
```

## 3. DataSource

```ts
export interface DataSource {
  listChecks(): LegacyCheck[];
  source(checkId: string): { file: string; text: string }[];
  subscribe(cb: (e: EngineEvent) => void): () => void;
  runRead(checkId: string): void;      // starts the Read playback
  runFind(checkId: string): void;      // replay + findings playback
  runProve(checkId: string): void;     // rules + verify + rounds playback
  acceptFinding(id: number, by: string): WorkOrder;
  dismissFinding(id: number, by: string, reason: string): void;
  signOff(checkId: string, by: string): void;
  acknowledgeHandoff(by: string): void;
  director: { restart(screen: 'read'|'find'|'prove'): void; jumpToEnd(screen: 'read'|'find'|'prove'): void; setSpeed(x: 1|2|5): void; toggle(flag: 'flaggedCard'|'blockedSignoff'|'nemotronOffline'|'cached', on: boolean): void };
}
```

`ApiDataSource` implements the same interface with `fetch`/WebSocket TODOs.

## 4. Playback scripts (timings at 1×)

**Read** (`runRead`): `Reading check_rack_inlet.cfg` 0.4 s → `Reading commands.cfg` 0.3 s → `Reading services.cfg` 0.3 s → `Cross-checking inventory.csv` 0.5 s → `Cross-checking oncall_roster.csv` 0.4 s → `Writing rule card` (Super, 3.2 s, timer visible) → card appears whole → execution check: statements verify one by one, 0.6 s apart, each with 2–4 runs (`26.9 → OK ✓`, `27.1 → WARNING ✓`, `32.1 → CRITICAL ✓`, `-0.1 → CRITICAL ✓`). With `flaggedCard` on, the critical-threshold statement first says 30 °C, flags at 32, and shows `corrected`.

**Find** (`runFind`): replay progress bar 0 → 100% over 2.5 s with the plugin-run counter climbing to 30,240 → `ReplaySummary` → detectors run 0.4 s apart (`neighbour-disagreement`, `inlet/outlet gap`, `cooling-effectiveness trend`, `periodic false alarm`, `inventory cross-check`, `roster cross-check`, `missing data`) → findings appear one by one, each after a 0.8 s `Nemotron Nano · writing` state. Final state: all six open (the demo click-path accepts 1, 2, 5 and dismisses 3). `jumpToEnd` applies those decisions.

**Prove** (`runProve`): `Generating rules` (Super, 2.8 s) → rules YAML appears → `promtool check rules ✓` → **one-shot column:** `Running verifier` 1.5 s → red strip + 3 counterexamples → **Gauntlet column:** round 1: 3 open → `Feeding counterexamples back` (Super 1.6 s) → round 2: 1 open → round 3: 0 → green strip → timing traces 500/500 → certificate (unsigned). With `blockedSignoff` on (for `check_ups_battery`), the Gauntlet column ends at 1 open and Sign off is disabled.

## 5. The recording (`recording.ts`)

Generate deterministically with `mulberry32(7)`, one point per 10 minutes for 21 days (3,024 points per series):
- `B7.reported` = 26 + noise(±0.3) + 10 from day 0; `B7.outlet` = 26 + 9 + noise; `B6.inlet`, `B8.inlet` = 24–26 + noise
- `CU-B.coolingPerKw` = 1.00 sloping to 0.85 over 21 days; `CU-B.status` = 1 constant
- `C.rowMeanInlet` = 23 + 2 × spike at 02:00–02:40 daily, max 29.5
- `A4.timeoutsPerDay` = 3–6 per day
- Legacy page ticks: B7 CRITICAL every 3 min for the first 42 minutes each day (re-notification), row C nightly; total 214 with 196 on B7.

## 6. Determinism

No `Math.random()`. Playback uses `setTimeout` chains driven by a speed multiplier; `restart` clears them; `jumpToEnd` emits the final events synchronously. Support `?seek=end` on any screen URL for screenshots.
